# Quick Start - Package Inline Edit

## Installation en 6 étapes

### 1️⃣ Ajouter le repository dans [composer.json](file:///Users/mac/Documents/PROJETS/money_transfer_app/backend/composer.json)

```json
{
    "repositories": [
        {
            "type": "path",
            "url": "../money_transfer_app/backend/packages/inline-edit"
        }
    ],
    "require": {
        "money-transfer/inline-edit": "@dev"
    }
}
```

### 2️⃣ Installer

```bash
composer update money-transfer/inline-edit
```

### 3️⃣ Publier les assets

```bash
php artisan vendor:publish --tag=inline-edit-assets
php artisan vendor:publish --tag=inline-edit-config
```

### 4️⃣ Configurer le modèle

```php
use MoneyTransfer\InlineEdit\Traits\HasInlineEdit;

class Transaction extends Model
{
    use HasInlineEdit;
    
    protected $inlineEditableFields = ['name', 'status'];
}
```

### 5️⃣ Ajouter la route

```php
// routes/api.php
use MoneyTransfer\InlineEdit\Http\Controllers\InlineEditController;

Route::middleware('auth:sanctum')->patch('/{model}/{id}', 
    [InlineEditController::class, 'update']
);
```

### 6️⃣ Utiliser dans la vue

```html
<head>
    <meta name="csrf-token" content="{{ csrf_token() }}">
    <link href="{{ asset('css/inline-edit.css') }}" rel="stylesheet">
</head>
<body>
    <span class="editable-field" data-id="1" data-field="name">
        John Doe
    </span>

    <script src="{{ asset('js/inline-edit.js') }}"></script>
    <script>
        initInlineEdit({
            selector: '.editable-field',
            apiEndpoint: '/api/transactions'
        });
    </script>
</body>
```

## ✅ Terminé !

Double-cliquez sur un champ pour l'éditer. Appuyez sur Entrée pour sauvegarder.
